/-! # Ordinary offset-180: row-one coefficient four is a shadow

The complementary I3 lane left one exact lower-jet scalar at contracted
coefficient `2` (expanded `120`).  Here we consume contracted row-one
coefficient `4` (expanded `299`).  After its literal I3 loads cancel, the
row is the six-term edge core displayed below.  That core is already in the
ideal generated by the face, discriminant, cusp pin and three joined first
jets, so this row is derivative-dependent and gives no new scalar.  The I3
coefficient-`2` residual is retained verbatim.  The next unused complementary
source row is row-two coefficient `4` (expanded `299`).
-/

